.TH WEILER\-PACK\-DATA 6 2026-11-25 "Weiler 0.1.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
weiler\-pack\-data \- build the local package weiler\-data from the game data of the Gold Edition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weiler\-pack\-data
.br
.B weiler\-pack\-data
.B \-\-source
.I folder\fR|\fIimage
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR folder ]
.RB [ \-\-music ]
.RB [ \-\-install ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B weiler\-pack\-data
builds the Debian package
.I weiler\-data_1.0_all.deb
from your own copy of the Gold Edition, so that
.BR weiler (6)
finds the game data for all users of the computer in
.IR /usr/share/games/weiler\-data .
The package contains only the files Weiler loads (listed in
.IR /usr/share/games/weiler/gamedata.list ),
in upper case names, and optionally the music of the CD.
It is meant for this computer only: the game data is not free and must not be passed on.
.PP
Without options on a terminal the program checks the tools it needs (and offers to install missing ones with
apt), asks for the folder or CD image, shows what it found, builds the package and offers to install it.
.PP
A folder is searched with all its sub folders for the game folder (the one with DATA and GFX); the case of the
names does not matter.
CD images are read with
.BR bchunk (1)
and
.BR 7z (1):
.IR .iso ,
CloneCD
.RI ( .ccd
with
.IR .img )
and
.I .cue
with
.IR .bin .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-source " folder" \fR|\fIimage
Folder with the game data or above it, or a CD image.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " folder"
Folder for the package (default: the current folder).
.TP
.B \-\-music
Include the audio tracks of the CD, converted to Ogg Vorbis by
.BR "weiler \-\-cd\-music" .
Needs a
.I .ccd
or
.I .cue
image; for a folder, an image in or next to it is used.
.TP
.B \-\-install
Install the package afterwards (apt, with sudo if not run as root).
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Answer all questions with yes, e.g. install missing tools.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors, 2 on wrong usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
weiler\-pack\-data \-\-source /media/cdrom \-\-install
weiler\-pack\-data \-\-source ~/S2GOLD.ccd \-\-music \-\-output ~/pakete
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR weiler (6),
.BR dpkg\-deb (1),
.BR bchunk (1),
.BR 7z (1)
